<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
        <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
        <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
        <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
        <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
        <AnalysisLevel>latest</AnalysisLevel>
        <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>true</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
        <EnforceExtendedAnalyzerRules>true</EnforceExtendedAnalyzerRules>
        <RunAnalyzersDuringBuild>true</RunAnalyzersDuringBuild>
        <RunAnalyzersDuringLiveAnalysis>true</RunAnalyzersDuringLiveAnalysis>
        <CodeAnalysisTreatWarningsAsErrors>true</CodeAnalysisTreatWarningsAsErrors>
    </PropertyGroup>
    <PropertyGroup>
        <!-- Required for deterministic, source-linked packages from local and CI builds. -->
        <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
        <!-- Keep one lock file valid for solution restore and the linux-x64 trim test. -->
        <RuntimeIdentifiers>linux-x64</RuntimeIdentifiers>
        <ContinuousIntegrationBuild>true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
        <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
        <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
        <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
        <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    </PropertyGroup>
    <PropertyGroup>
        <PackageId>FriendlyEnvars</PackageId>
        <VersionPrefix>2.0.0</VersionPrefix>
        <!-- Prerelease for the 2.0 review; the 2.0.0 release removes the suffix. -->
        <VersionSuffix>alpha</VersionSuffix>
        <PackageReleaseNotes>
## Intentional breaking changes in 2.0.0

- EnvarsException is sealed and carries structured failure metadata. Library-generated failures omit
  values, cause messages and inner exceptions. OperationCanceledException is propagated unchanged.
- The options-blocking methods were removed. All standard Options abstractions resolve normally.
- BindEnvars now validates property shapes and environment names, even when a variable is absent.
- Registering FriendlyEnvars twice for the same options type and name throws InvalidOperationException.
- BindEnvars captures values once. Later environment changes do not affect any Options abstraction.
- A non-flags enum rejects numeric "-1" even when All = -1 is declared.
- A non-flags enum rejects "Read,Write" even when ReadWrite = 3 is declared.
- A flags enum rejects negative numeric text but accepts the declared member name. Ambiguous names and
  bit patterns with undeclared bits are also rejected.
- BindEnvars&lt;T&gt; preserves public properties for trimmed applications.
- BindEnvars clones and freezes the configured culture.

## Not new in 2.0

- Empty strings have been passed to the binder since 1.1.0. They are not a 2.0 change.

## Other changes

- XML documentation is generated and packaged.
- Lambdas that capture no state are marked static, reducing allocations.
- New package icon.
        </PackageReleaseNotes>
        <Authors>Lukasz Lepecki</Authors>
        <Description>Binds environment variables to strongly typed .NET options.</Description>
        <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
        <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
        <PackageTags>configuration;options;environment-variables</PackageTags>
        <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 Lukasz Lepecki</Copyright>
        <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/llepecki/friendly-envars</PackageProjectUrl>
        <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/llepecki/friendly-envars</RepositoryUrl>
        <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
        <PackageIcon>icon-v2.png</PackageIcon>
        <GeneratePackageOnBuild>false</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
        <EnablePackageValidation>true</EnablePackageValidation>
        <PackageValidationBaselineVersion>1.1.0</PackageValidationBaselineVersion>
    </PropertyGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
        <AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleTo">
            <_Parameter1>FriendlyEnvars.Tests</_Parameter1>
        </AssemblyAttribute>
    </ItemGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
        <ApiCompatSuppressionFile Include="CompatibilitySuppressions.xml" />
    </ItemGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
        <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
        <None Include="..\..\resources\icon-v2.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    </ItemGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
        <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options" Version="8.0.2" />
    </ItemGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
        <PackageReference Include="SonarAnalyzer.CSharp" Version="10.19.0.132793">
            <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
            <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
        </PackageReference>
        <PackageReference Include="Roslynator.Analyzers" Version="4.15.0">
            <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
            <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
        </PackageReference>
        <PackageReference Include="Nullable.Extended.Analyzer" Version="1.15.6581">
            <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
            <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
        </PackageReference>
        <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="8.0.0">
            <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
            <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
        </PackageReference>
    </ItemGroup>
</Project>
